agent: Refuse connections from where agents' work runs

On a machine whose agents run as the person's own account, the socket,
open to the account, serves them every key the agent holds. Read a
gate, a file named by SSH_TPM_AGENT_GATE, at each connection, and refuse
a peer when the first process of its chain, itself and then each parent,
whose cgroup a rule names is refused there. Allow ends the search, so a
terminal can be allowed inside a slice that is refused. A refused peer
hears "refused" for every request, and the journal names its unit and
folder. watch journals what would be refused and serves it. A gate that
can't be read or parsed, or a peer the kernel doesn't name, is refused.
Where the variable is unset, nothing changes.

